  "id": "Compound::DB00796 - Gene::185",
  "verbalization": "Candesartan is closely related to other angiotensin II receptor antagonists, such as Valsartan and Forasartan, through a shared structural profile and pharmacological similarity. These compounds bind to the Agtr1 receptor, which is a key target in the renin-angiotensin system. The evidence suggests that Candesartan, through its structural resemblance to other angiotensin II receptor antagonists, may exert its effects by interacting with Agtr1, potentially modulating receptor activity. The lowest common ancestors of Candesartan and its analogs point to broader classes like Angiotensin II Receptor Antagonists and Tetrazoles, which may provide a mechanistic framework for its action. The binding of Forasartan to Agtr1 is consistently highlighted across the paths, reinforcing the hypothesis that Candesartan may similarly interact with this receptor. The evidence supports a mechanism involving receptor binding, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
